# Python bytecode. One pattern rather than one line per directory: the
# per-directory list silently stopped covering anything when app/retrieval and
# tests/retrieval were added, and 34 .pyc files went into the staging area.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist/assets
.DS_Store

# Local configuration. Holds API keys once grey-literature retrieval is
# configured, so it must never be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Retrieved data: WARC archives and the retrieval database. Under DATA_DIR in
# Docker, here for a checkout run without it — the runs live in DATA_DIR/runs,
# which for a local checkout is backend/data/runs.
backend/data/

# Database backups. Written to the checkout root because that is where the
# shell happens to be, which is how a 3 MB tarball of reviq.db — a review's
# papers, its reviewers and their addresses — reached a public repository. The
# pattern is broader than that one filename on purpose: nothing this project
# ships is a tarball, so the rule costs nothing and does not depend on the next
# backup being named the same way.
*.tar.gz
